# The Go images copy go.mod, go.sum, the Go sources in this directory,
# and cli/, and nothing else. Everything below is documentation, plans,
# manifests, test data, smoke scripts, generated skills, a workstation's
# build output, or the source of an image with its own context (the
# media browser's Rust tree, `appearances`, `titles`, and Corrosion). Sending any
# of it to the daemon costs the build time and no Go build reads it. A
# change to any of it must not rebuild the Go images, and CI selects
# images by what this file leaves in. The cargo target directory is the
# large one, gigabytes on a workstation.
deploy
docs
plans
testdata
local
media-browser
appearances
titles
corrosion
skills
smoke
coverage.out
coverage-media-browser.xml
README.md
LICENSE
/library-operator
# The report of the pins of the appearances image and the titles image,
# which runs on a workstation and never in a build.
latest.sh
# The manifest of those two images' pins. Only they read it, through
# Dockerfile.appearances.dockerignore and Dockerfile.titles.dockerignore,
# so a bump of OpenVINO rebuilds no Go image.
pin.toml
